# Findings in history that are not leaks. One line per fingerprint, which is
# commit:path:rule:line, so an entry stops applying the moment the line moves
# and the moment the history is rewritten, because a rewrite reissues every
# commit and the hash in the entry is no longer one that exists.
#
# This file is not the place to silence a real credential. A secret that
# reached a commit is disclosed even after the line is deleted, because the
# commit keeps it; the response is to rotate the credential and then rewrite or
# abandon the history, not to add a line here.

